Correct answer: $\boxed{2:1}$.  Hence $p+q=\boxed{3}$.

Explanation:  The length of the altitude of trapezoid $ABYX$ is $12$ while the length of the altitude of trapezoid $XYCD$ is $12/2=6$.  Moreover, the area of trapezoid $YZBC$ is $1/2\times 12\times PQ$ while the area of trapezoid $YZAD$ is $1/2\times 12\times PQ/2$, yielding $6:3$ as the area ratio.  In total, $p:q=2:1$ as desired.
[asy]
import olympiad;
pair A, B, C, D, O, P, X, Y;
A= (6, 8);
B=(18, 8);
C=(24, 0);
D=(0,0);
O=(12,0);
P=(12,8);
X=(A+D)/2;
Y=(B+C)/2;
draw(X--Y, dashed);
draw(A--B--C--D--A);
draw(A--O--B);
draw(O--P, dashed);

label("A", A, NW);
label("B", B, NE);
label("C", C, SE);
label("D", D, SW);
label("O", O, S);
label("P", P, N);
label("X", X, NW);
label("Y", Y, NE);

dot((6,0));

dot((9,2*sqrt(6)));
label("S", (9,2*sqrt(6)), E);

dot((15,4*sqrt(6)));
label("T", (15,4*sqrt(6)), E);

dot((0,4*sqrt(6)));
label("T", (0,4*sqrt(6)), E);

dot((12,0));
label("O", (12,0), S);

dot((6,8));
label("B", (6,8), N);

dot((18,8));
label("A", (18,8), N);

dot((0,0));
label("D", (0,0), SW);

dot((24,0));
label("C", (24,0), SE);
[/asy]
$ABYX$ is similar to $XYCD$. Therefore, the ratio of the area of $ABYX$ to the area of $XYCD$ is the ratio of the squares of the sides, which is $\frac{3^2}{6^2}=\frac{1}{4}$.  The ratio of the areas is $1:4$, so the desired answer is $p+q=\boxed{3}$.

